From 5a8b8b9ac82ac17c6352352e94b70fb52d6328b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: StonkGuy <68372320+StonkGuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 07:25:50 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] Add an in-process sampling profiler (FEX_PROFILESAMPLEHZ)

Anti-cheat clients detect debuggers and `perf`, so a game under one cannot be profiled from outside. This adds a
statistical sampler that lives entirely inside the emulator process: a host thread sends SIGPROF to the busy guest threads
while /dev/shm/fex-<pid>-sample-on exists; a host signal handler records {host PC, tid, last guest RIP} into
/dev/shm/fex-<pid>-samples. With FEX_LIBRARYJITNAMING=1 the host PCs resolve to guest libraries through
/tmp/perf-<pid>.map, and to FEX functions with an unstripped FEX binary.

The sampler only starts in a process that grows past 100 guest threads (the application, not the hundreds of helper FEX
processes of a Wine session), creates its record file lazily on the first trigger, and stands down while a ptrace tracer
is attached (it would see every SIGPROF).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
